course: dictionary
lesson: 4120
title: Body parts and what they make
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gland is a small part of your body that makes a special substance your body needs. You may not know the word, but the sentences around it give clues. «Kneading... leaves scent from glands in the paws.» Leaving scent is something that comes out, so a gland must make something that leaves the body.
explain: «Dogs sniff each other's bottoms to say hello, because special scent glands there tell who the other dog is.» The word scent tells you the gland makes a smell. Ask yourself: what would fit in place of glands? Then try your idea in the sentence: a special smell-maker there tells who the other dog is. It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «The Komodo dragon... has venom glands in its jaw.» Venom is poison, so venom glands make poison. Swap in your meaning: the dragon has poison-makers in its jaw. That fits the sentence, so you can trust your guess.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. In a doctor's office, «swollen glands» means the small lumps in your neck that grow bigger when you are fighting an illness. Context helps, but when you are not sure, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A gland is a small part of the body that makes a special substance, such as sweat, saliva, tears or hormones.
fact: «Swollen glands» usually means the small lumps in the neck that get bigger when you are fighting an illness.
fact: Sweat glands cool the skin, and salivary glands make spit to help digest food.
fact: Tear glands keep the eyes wet, and glands like the thyroid make hormones that control growth.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Kneading... leaves scent from glands in the paws.» What is a gland? | A bone in the leg | A soft blanket for kittens | *A small part of the body that makes a special substance
exercise: A doctor may feel your neck for swollen glands when you have a sore throat. What are swollen glands? | A kind of sore throat medicine | Long, thin bones in the neck | *Small lumps in the neck that get bigger when you are fighting an illness
exercise: «The Komodo dragon... has venom glands in its jaw.» What do venom glands make? | *Poison | Sweat | Tears | Hormones for growth
exercise: Which glands make spit to help digest food? | Scent glands | Sweat glands | *Salivary glands | Tear glands
test: Which glands keep your eyes wet? | *Tear glands | Scent glands | Sweat glands | Salivary glands
test: «Around puberty special sweat glands in the armpits switch on.» What does «switch on» most likely mean? | Turn off | *Start working | Fall asleep | Break down
exam: «Dogs sniff each other's bottoms to say hello, because special scent glands there tell who the other dog is.» What do scent glands do? | Keep the eyes wet | *Make a smell that tells who the other dog is | Make spit to help digest food | Cool the skin
